network-manager-openvpn3 (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Store the profile as a system-owned connection secret: before, any
    local user could read the private key with nmcli. Existing connections
    are moved on upgrade.
  * Document the connection format and how to add a front-end for another
    desktop, with a conformance suite front-ends run against the core.
  * Split the sources into the core (libnm-plugin/) and the GTK front-end
    (frontends/gtk/); the core package no longer pulls in GTK.
  * Recognise remotes inside <connection> blocks.
  * Write exported profiles with mode 0600.
  * Say why a connection ended (e.g. the server expired the session), do
    not disconnect a session openvpn3 already ended, log logins asked for
    during a session and where a connection was when it was stopped.

 -- AlexeySetevoi <17676189+AlexeySetevoi@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

network-manager-openvpn3 (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Web based login: open the server's login URL in the desktop user's
    browser (through xdg-desktop-portal) and wait for the server.
  * PKCS#12 client credentials: the bundle is kept in the connection and
    converted to PEM for openvpn3 when connecting.
  * Encrypted private keys: passphrase as a NetworkManager secret.
  * GTK 3 editor for nm-connection-editor next to the GTK 4 one.
  * Keep login URLs out of the journal.

 -- AlexeySetevoi <17676189+AlexeySetevoi@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0000

